# Every ignore here needs a reason — see .checkov.yaml's header for why.

# The security-alerts SNS topics (root sign-in + break-glass alerts, see
# live/aws/org-management/alarms.tf) use the AWS-managed key, not a dedicated
# CMK. They carry only "someone signed in as root/break-glass" notifications —
# operational alerts, not sensitive data — and a per-topic CMK is an ongoing
# key policy and rotation to maintain for a low-value target.
AVD-AWS-0136
